---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Заголовок -->
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium mb-3" style="color: #a78bfa; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        The Problem
      </p>
      <h2
        class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-4"
        style="color: #e8e8ed; letter-spacing: -0.02em;"
      >
        What's actually broken in 2026
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base max-w-2xl mx-auto" style="color: #8888a0; line-height: 1.7;">
        AI Overviews now appear on nearly half of all Google searches. Your clients' traffic is down 30–60% and they're asking what you're doing about it. Your current workflow: three paid tools, a folder of ad-hoc prompts, and a GitHub repo someone bookmarked last year that hasn't been updated since.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Проблемы-карточки -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-14">
      {[
        {
          stat: '48%',
          label: 'of Google queries now show AI Overviews',
          icon: 'spark',
          color: '#7c5cff',
        },
        {
          stat: '4–8h',
          label: 'wasted per week on repetitive SEO tasks',
          icon: 'clock',
          color: '#a78bfa',
        },
        {
          stat: '$0',
          label: 'structured AI workflow for most agencies',
          icon: 'settings',
          color: '#3ddc97',
        },
      ].map((item) => (
        <div
          class="text-center p-6 rounded-xl"
          style="background: #111118; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);"
        >
          <div
            class="mx-auto mb-3 inline-flex items-center justify-center"
            style={`width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 10px; background: ${item.color}1f; border: 1px solid ${item.color}33;`}
          >
            <Icon name={item.icon} color={item.color} size={22} />
          </div>
          <div
            class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1"
            style="color: #e8e8ed; letter-spacing: -0.03em;"
          >
            {item.stat}
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm" style="color: #8888a0;">{item.label}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Решение -->
    <div
      class="relative p-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden"
      style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(124,92,255,0.08) 0%, rgba(61,220,151,0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(124,92,255,0.2);"
    >
      <p class="text-sm font-medium mb-3" style="color: #3ddc97; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        The Solution
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: #e8e8ed; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        A pipeline. Not another pile of prompts.
      </h3>
      <p class="text-base" style="color: #8888a0; max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.7;">
        Every free SEO skill repo is a collection. You load one skill, get an output, and manually decide what to do next. That's fine for experiments. It's not fine when you bill $5k–$15k a month and need to ship audits consistently. SkillsForge is different: each skill knows about the others. One prompt — "optimize this cluster for GEO" — runs the whole chain.
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-6 text-xs overflow-x-auto" style="color: #8888a0; line-height: 1.5;">keyword-cluster-mapper → content-brief-builder → seo-pseo-generator
                              ↓
                       geo-aeo-optimizer → schema-markup-engineer
                              ↓
                  internal-linking-architect → technical-seo-auditor
                              ↓
                  backlink-outreach-engine → ai-mentions-monitor</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
